## 6️⃣ Extending Without Loops (Optional)

If you later decide you really want **zero loops** (i.e., the program runs once and then exits), you can wrap everything in a single `main()` function and rely on an external timer or keyboard interrupt to restart. That level of complexity isn’t covered here, but the principle remains: **avoid `while(true)` around motor commands**.

